Vendor log samples harvested from third-party corpora
=====================================================

The sample documents contain real vendor log lines copied from upstream test
fixtures. They are NOT written by hand and NOT generated by a model; each file
records where its lines came from:

    "upstream": { "repo": …, "commit": …, "path": …, "license": … }

The documents themselves live in the samples POOL repository, not in this one —
see src/samples-pool.ts. This NOTICE ships with the app because the attribution
has to travel with the reader as well as with the data, and because
config/samples-pool-index.json (which does ship here) describes that corpus.

Each corpus below owns the files whose index row carries its id, and states its
own terms. Removing a corpus's section while its files are still published would
breach the attribution every one of these licences requires.

