Regenerating
------------
  attack_data npm run samples:harvest:attackdata -- --promote
  elastic  npm run samples:harvest -- --promote
  logtest  npm run samples:harvest:logtests -- --promote
  logtest_extras npm run samples:harvest:logtests -- --promote
  sc4s     npm run samples:harvest:sc4s -- --promote

Every harvest is pinned to a commit, so re-running reproduces the same files,
and each one rewrites only its own corpus. Deleting a sample is a normal, safe
fix: resolution falls through to the next tier. Do not edit the log lines
themselves — an edited line is neither the real vendor format nor traceable to
upstream.
